 "final_text": "Submitted:\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| `jan_erp_ap` | $13,800 |\n| `jan_workbook_ap` | $12,000 |\n| `jan_variance` | $1,800 |\n\n**Root cause of the variance:** the workbook (`CESQ-close-workbook-2026-01.xlsx`) was locked on 1/27, one day before QINV\u2011002 ($1,800, \"January late-posted repair\") hit the AP subledger on 1/28. The workbook's own note flags this \u2014 \"QINV-001 only; prepared 01-27\" \u2014 so it's a timing gap, not a data error. Both open invoices are unsettled and dated within the January period (2026-01-01\u201301-31 per FiscalPeriods, status: closed); the $3,200 QINV-003 is a February transaction and correctly excluded from both sides.\n\nReady for February whenever you want to continue.\n\n[step 02] Submitted:\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| `feb_erp_ap` | $17,000 |\n| `feb_workbook_ap` | $13,800 |\n| `feb_variance` | $3,200 |\n| `jan_item_resolved` | yes |\n\n**Summary:** January's culprit (QINV\u2011002, the late-posted repair invoice) is now correctly reflected in the February workbook \u2014 that gap is closed. However, a *new* gap opened up: QINV\u2011003 ($3,200, February facilities services, posted 2/25) is missing from the workbook even though it posted before the workbook's 2/26 prep date. Worth flagging to Jordan Blake \u2014 this looks like a recurring pattern of the workbook lagging by one late/near-cutoff invoice each period rather than a one-off.",
